      "message": "Give the inbox, tasks and agents their rows and cards\n\nThe inbox groups its notices by day, each a row with the unread dot,\nthe actor drawn, the sentence, where it happened, a chip naming what\nkind of thing it is, and the time. Tasks are rows behind filter pills\nfor state and, when the sidebar names more than one repository, for\nrepository; each row carries a state chip, the title, where it lives,\nwho holds it, and the avatars of those who took it; the lessons that\nattempts left behind sit under the list. A task's own page opens like\na change's: title, state chip, who filed it, who holds it, the change\nit produced; then the specification, attempts as cards side by side,\nreadiness as the same rows the change page uses, sessions, and the\nchanges that named it, with closing it behind two buttons in the head.\n\nAgents are cards two to a row: the avatar, the display name, the id,\nmodel, harness and owner beneath it, New token and Retire on the right\nfor an agent that is yours; then what it can do as chips per grant with\nwhere and a Revoke, its record in counts rather than a percentage, what\nit is doing now, and granting something folded behind a control. Adding\nan agent is a form of fields with the model hint. The lessons page is\nthe same rows as everywhere else, with its search beside the heading.\n\nEvery page names people by display name and draws them; the routes\nlook everyone up once through one helper.\n\nChange-Id: Iwork0130a\nTask: t-3b7v4s0v6y1pe88ft9m4t6aewm\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
